## Tech stack

- **Flutter** (iOS + Android), Material 3 with light/dark themes from design tokens
- **flutter_riverpod**: state management (`Notifier` / `AsyncNotifier`)
- **go_router**: navigation, one router in `lib/app/router.dart`
- **shared_preferences** <+ the PRD's storage: drift / sqflite / flutter_secure_storage>: local persistence behind repositories
- <dio | Firebase: only if the app has a backend>
- **flutter_localizations** + **intl**: localization (<locales>)

## Architecture

Feature-first layout:

```
lib/
  main.dart                 startup: error handlers -> storage -> orientation -> runApp
  app/                      App (MaterialApp.router), router, bootstrap (opens storage)
  core/
    config/app_config.dart  every tunable constant (timeouts, page sizes, limits)
    theme/                  design tokens + light/dark ThemeData
    services/               shared clients and storage providers
    widgets/                AsyncValueView, EmptyView, ErrorView
  features/<feature>/
    data/                   models + repository (the only code that touches storage/network)
    presentation/           screens, widgets, notifiers
  l10n/                     app_<locale>.arb
```

Widgets read state from Riverpod providers. Notifiers call repositories. Repositories own
storage and network access. Tests swap a repository through `ProviderScope` /
`ProviderContainer` overrides.

## Run

```bash
flutter pub get
flutter run
```

## Test & analyze

```bash
flutter analyze
flutter test                                    # unit + widget tests
flutter test integration_test -d <device-id>    # primary flow on a simulator/emulator
```

## Build (release)

```bash
flutter build ipa          # iOS
flutter build appbundle    # Android
```

